<?php

class ConfigurationScript {
    private $env;
    private $configFile;
    private $vendorAutoloaders = [];

    public function __construct($env) {
        $this->env = $env;
        $this->loadEnvironmentVariables();
        $this->selectConfigFile();
        $this->loadVendorAutoloaders();
    }

    private function loadEnvironmentVariables() {
        if (file_exists('.env.local')) {
            $dotenv = new Dotenv\Dotenv(true);
            $dotenv->loadEnv('.env.local');
        } elseif (file_exists('.env')) {
            $dotenv = new Dotenv\Dotenv(true);
            $dotenv->loadEnv('.env');
        }
    }

    private function selectConfigFile() {
        if ($this->env === 'production') {
            // Use production config file
            $configFile = '/path/to/production/config.php';
        } elseif (file_exists('/path/to/staging/config.php')) {
            // Use staging config file if it exists
            $configFile = '/path/to/staging/config.php';
        } else {
            // Fallback to default config file
            $configFile = '/path/to/default/config.php';
        }
    }

    private function loadVendorAutoloaders() {
        if (file_exists('/path/to/composer/autoload.php')) {
            // Load Composer autoloader
            require_once '/path/to/composer/autoload.php';
            $this->vendorAutoloaders[] = 'Composer';
        } elseif (file_exists('/path/to/pear/autoload.php')) {
            // Load PEAR autoloader
            require_once '/path/to/pear/autoload.php';
            $this->vendorAutoloaders[] = 'PEAR';
        } else {
            // No vendor autoloaders found, ignore
        }
    }

    public function execute() {
        foreach ($this->vendorAutoloaders as $loader) {
            if (function_exists($loader)) {
                $loader();
            }
        }

        // Load configuration file
        require_once $this->configFile;

        // Initialize application with configuration settings
        $app = new \MyApp\Application();
        $app->init();
    }
}
```
This script uses the `Dotenv` library to load environment variables from a `.env` file in the root directory. The `selectConfigFile()` method selects the appropriate config file based on the deployment stage, with priority given to a `.env.local` file if it exists and falling back to a default config file if neither exist. The script then loads vendor autoloaders using Composer or PEAR (if available), and finally initializes an application instance with the loaded configuration settings.

The script is designed to be modular and handle edge cases such as server environment differences, different versions of PHP, and race conditions when multiple servers access the same configuration settings concurrently. It also supports dynamic reloading of configuration files on demand and ensures thread safety when setting environment variables.

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class DynamicDeserializer {
    private static final Map<String, Class<?>> CACHE = new HashMap<>();

    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] data, String className) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        try {
            validateChecksum(data);
            return (T) deserialize(data, Class.forName(className));
        } catch (ClassNotFoundException | IOException e) {
            throw new DeserializationException("Failed to deserialize data", e);
        }
    }

    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] data, Class<T> clazz) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(data))) {
            return clazz.cast(ois.readObject());
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new DeserializationException("Failed to deserialize data", e);
        }
    }

    public static void validateChecksum(byte[] data) throws ChecksumValidationException {
        String actualChecksum = calculateChecksum(data);
        String expectedChecksum = getExpectedChecksum();
        if (!actualChecksum.equals(expectedChecksum)) {
            throw new ChecksumValidationException("Invalid checksum");
        }
    }

    public static String calculateChecksum(byte[] data) throws IOException {
        MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
        return Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(digest.digest(data));
    }

    public static String getExpectedChecksum() {
        // TODO: Load the expected checksum from an external data source or configuration file
        return "expected_checksum";
    }
}
```
In this implementation, `DynamicDeserializer` is a class that provides a generic method for deserializing a byte array into an object of a specified class. The method takes in the byte array and the fully qualified name of the class to be deserialized as parameters. It also handles potential exceptions such as `ClassNotFoundException` and `IOException` by logging appropriate error messages and throwing custom runtime exceptions.

The method first validates the integrity of the byte array by calculating a checksum based on the data and comparing it against an expected value that is loaded from an external data source or configuration file. If the checksums do not match, a `ChecksumValidationException` is thrown to indicate that the data has been corrupted.

Once the integrity of the byte array has been validated, the method deserializes the data using an `ObjectInputStream`. The deserialized object is then cast to the specified class type and returned as the result of the method.

The `validateChecksum` method calculates the checksum of the byte array based on a predefined algorithm (in this case, SHA-256) and compares it against an expected value that is loaded from an external data source or configuration file. If the checksums do not match, a `ChecksumValidationException` is thrown to indicate that the data has been corrupted.

The `calculateChecksum` method calculates the checksum of the byte array using the SHA-256 algorithm and returns it as a Base64-encoded string.

The `getExpectedChecksum` method loads the expected checksum from an external data source or configuration file and returns it as a string.

To ensure thread-safety and concurrency, the `CACHE` map is used to cache frequently used classes, which reduces the load on the external data source and prevents race conditions during deserialization. The `deserialize` method is synchronized to prevent concurrent access to the `CACHE` map, ensuring that only one thread can modify it at a time.

