This function takes three arguments: `moduleName` (a string representing the name of the module to be tested), `testCases` (an array of functions where each function represents a test case), and `setUpFunction` (an optional function to set up any necessary resources before running the tests). It loads the module using the `require` function, runs all test cases in the `testCases` array, and resets the mocking library `blueslip` after each test. The function also logs detailed information to the console, including the name of the module being tested, the name of each test case, and any errors encountered during the test execution.

The function uses a try-catch block to handle potential errors gracefully, provides informative error messages, and includes robust error handling and edge case management. It also incorporates performance optimization and scalability considerations, especially when dealing with a large number of test cases. Additionally, it implements resource management and cleanup strategies to ensure that all resources used during test execution are properly released and do not cause memory leaks or other issues.

