```
function copyBytes(bufferList, numBytes) {
  // Create a new buffer for the copied bytes
  const newBuffer = Buffer.alloc(numBytes);

  // Iterate over each chunk in the buffer list
  let totalBytesCopied = 0;
  bufferList.forEach((chunk) => {
    // Get the length of the current chunk
    const chunkLength = chunk.length;

    // Check if the chunk length is valid and if there is still space left in the new buffer
    if (chunkLength > numBytes - totalBytesCopied || totalBytesCopied >= numBytes) {
      throw new Error(`Invalid chunk length: ${chunkLength}. Total bytes copied: ${totalBytesCopied}.`);
    }

    // Copy the current chunk into the new buffer, starting from the total number of bytes copied
    chunk.copy(newBuffer, totalBytesCopied);

    // Update the total number of bytes copied
    totalBytesCopied += chunkLength;
  });

  return newBuffer;
}
```
This function uses the `forEach` method to iterate over each chunk in the buffer list. It checks that each chunk has a valid length and that there is still space left in the new buffer before copying it into the new buffer. If any of these conditions are not met, an error is thrown. Once all chunks have been copied, the function returns the new buffer with the copied bytes.

This function uses `Buffer.alloc` to create a new buffer for the copied bytes, and it uses the `copy` method of each chunk to copy its contents into the new buffer. It also keeps track of the total number of bytes copied using the `totalBytesCopied` variable, and it throws an error if the total number of bytes copied exceeds the requested number of bytes or if there is no more space left in the new buffer.

