This code implements a scalable C# middleware component for a web application that dynamically updates specific HTML elements on a webpage via HTTP POST requests. The middleware uses multiple compression algorithms (such as GZIP, DEFLATE, and LZ4) to compress the data before sending it to a remote database server. The compressed data is stored temporarily in a memory-efficient manner and released promptly after use to prevent memory leaks.

The middleware also implements a caching mechanism for frequently used algorithms to enhance selection speed and includes a resumable file transfer mechanism to ensure data integrity during interrupted connections. The middleware discovers and connects to at least three different CMS providers (WordPress, Drupal, and custom-built CMSs) based on configuration settings.

The middleware also implements error handling mechanisms to handle unexpected errors that may occur while processing the request.

