The `FetchData` class has a single method `fetch`, which takes a URL as input and returns the response from the remote API as a string. This method uses the `makeRequest` method to make an HTTP request to the API, and then updates the UI with the response data using the `updateUI` method.

The `makeRequest` method first checks if there is cached data for the URL. If there is, it returns the cached data. Otherwise, it makes a new HTTP request using the `HttpURLConnection` class. It sets the request method to "GET", connects to the API, and reads the response as a string. If the status code of the response is 200 (OK), it caches the response and returns it. If the status code is not 200, it handles different types of errors by throwing exceptions or returning empty responses.

The `updateUI` method updates the UI with the response data from the API. It can be implemented in a separate class that handles the UI updates.

