The `verifyHash` method takes two string parameters representing the local file path and the cloud URL where the SHA-256 hash of the file will be verified. It calculates the SHA-256 hash of the local file using the `calculateSHA256Hash` method, and then compares it with the SHA-256 hash stored in the cloud. If the hashes match, the method returns true, otherwise it returns false.

