The `readFileAndProcessRecords()` function is defined in two parts. The first part reads the input file line by line and creates a new thread for each line using the lambda expression `[&](const std::string& line) {...}`. The second part of the function uses the mutex and condition variable to synchronize access to the output database and insert records into it concurrently.

