In the example usage of the `aesEncrypt` function, a plaintext message is encrypted using the ECB cipher mode with PKCS7 padding and PBKDF2 key derivation. The encrypted message is then printed to the console.

Note that this code assumes that the AES encryption library has been properly initialized and configured before calling the `aesEncrypt` function. It also assumes that the input parameters (key, initialization vector, cipher mode, padding scheme, and KDF) are valid and correctly set before using them in the encryption process.

