The `struct FactoryFunction` is used to represent a factory function that can create new instances of a transaction configuration. It contains the ID of the factory function, the number of fields it requires, and a list of field specifications that describe each field.

The `struct TransactionConfig` is used to represent an instance of a transaction configuration. It contains the ID of the transaction configuration, as well as the values of each field in the configuration.

The `generate` function takes a registry and an ID of a factory function, and it uses that factory function to create a new instance of a transaction configuration. The `is_valid` function takes a registry and a transaction configuration, and it checks whether the transaction configuration is valid according to the factory function in the registry with the same ID as the configuration.

