  for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
    if (pthread_create(&threads[i], &attr, process_data_streams, NULL)) {
      fprintf(stderr, "Failed to create thread\n");
      return EXIT_FAILURE;
    }
  }
  pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);

  // Wait for the threads to finish and handle any exceptions that may occur
  for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
    void *status;
    if (pthread_join(threads[i], &status)) {
      fprintf(stderr, "Failed to join thread\n");
      return EXIT_FAILURE;
    }
    handle_exceptions("Thread exception", status);
  }

  // Clean up and exit the program
  pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);
  fclose(log.file);
  return EXIT_SUCCESS;
}
```
This is a complete program in C that uses multiple threads to fetch data from an API concurrently, caches frequently accessed data, and handles exceptions using a logging mechanism. The program takes no command line arguments and does not provide any output. The `API_ENDPOINT`, `REQUEST_HEADERS`, and `QUERY_PARAMETERS` are initialized in the main function, while the `log` structure is used to keep track of all interactions between the application and the remote API. The `cache` array is used to store frequently accessed data and the `threads` array is used to create and manage threads for processing multiple data streams concurrently.

