```java
import java.security.Key;
import java.util.Base64;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import io.jsonwebtoken.Jwts;
import io.jsonwebtoken.SignatureAlgorithm;

public static String generateJwt(String privateKey, String userName, List<String> roles) {
    Key key = new SecretKeySpec(privateKey.getBytes(), SignatureAlgorithm.HS256);
    return Jwts.builder().setSubject(userName).claim("roles", roles).signWith(key, SignatureAlgorithm.HS256).compact();
}
```
This function takes three parameters: `privateKey`, which is the private key retrieved from the KMS; `userName`, which is the name of the user making the request; and `roles`, which is a list of roles assigned to the user. The function uses the `Jwts` class provided by the `io.jsonwebtoken` library to generate a JWT, which is then signed with the private key using the HS256 algorithm.

