Here is a sample implementation of the `updateClinicStatus` PHP function:
```php
function updateClinicStatus($clinicId, $status) {
    // Validate input clinic ID
    if (!is_numeric($clinicId)) {
        throw new \InvalidArgumentException("Invalid clinic ID");
    }

    // Handle edge cases such as non-existent clinic IDs and invalid IP addresses
    $ipAddress = $_SERVER["REMOTE_ADDR"];
    if (!filter_var($ipAddress, FILTER_VALIDATE_IP)) {
        throw new \InvalidArgumentException("Invalid IP address");
    }

    // Validate input status
    if (!is_string($status) || !in_array($status, ["open", "closed"])) {
        throw new \InvalidArgumentException("Invalid status");
    }

    // Connect to the database and update the clinic status
    $db = new mysqli("localhost", "username", "password", "database");
    if ($db->connect_error) {
        throw new \RuntimeException("Error connecting to database");
    }

    $query = "UPDATE clinics SET status = ? WHERE id = ?";
    $stmt = $db->prepare($query);
    $stmt->bind_param("si", $status, $clinicId);
    $stmt->execute();
    $stmt->close();

    // Close the database connection
    $db->close();
}
```
