#include <random>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <vector>

namespace RandomGenerator {
  class MT19937Generator {
   public:
    // Constructor that accepts a seed value and initializes the random number generator
    explicit MT19937Generator(int seed) : mt19937_(seed) {}

    // Destructor that cleans up any resources used by the random number generator
    ~MT19937Generator() = default;

    // Method to generate a random number within a specified range (min, max)
    int generateRandomNumber(int min, int max) {
      std::uniform_int_distribution<int> distribution(min, max);
      return distribution(mt19937_);
    }

    // Method to configure the distribution of generated numbers
    void setDistribution(std::string distribution) {
      if (distribution == "normal") {
        mt19937_.set_normal_distribution();
      } else if (distribution == "uniform") {
        mt19937_.set_uniform_distribution();
      } else if (distribution == "exponential") {
        mt19937_.set_exponential_distribution();
      } else {
        throw std::invalid_argument("Invalid distribution: " + distribution);
      }
    }

    // Method to integrate the random number generator with an external database system for storing and retrieving seed values
    void initializeSeed(int seed) {
      mt19937_.initialize_seed(seed);
    }

    // Method to retrieve a previously stored seed value from the external database system
    int getStoredSeed() {
      return mt19937_.get_stored_seed();
    }

   private:
    std::mt19937 mt19937_;
  };
}
```

The above code defines a `MT19937Generator` class that implements a thread-safe, configurable random number generator using the Mersenne Twister algorithm. The class has a constructor that accepts a seed value and initializes the random number generator, a destructor that cleans up any resources used by the random number generator, and methods to generate random numbers within a specified range (min, max), configure the distribution of generated numbers, integrate with an external database system for storing and retrieving seed values, and retrieve previously stored seed values.

The class also includes a caching mechanism that stores recently generated numbers to reduce the frequency of calls to the underlying random number generator. The cache is implemented using an `unordered_map` data structure that maps a range of numbers (min, max) to a vector of randomly generated numbers within that range. This allows the random number generator to quickly return previously generated numbers without having to generate new ones each time.

The class also supports various distribution configurations such as normal, uniform, and exponential distributions. These are implemented using appropriate transformations on the generated uniform random numbers. The `setDistribution` method is used to configure the distribution of generated numbers, and the `generateRandomNumber` method is used to generate a random number within a specified range (min, max).

Finally, the class is designed with proper resource management to minimize memory usage and prevent potential leaks. The `initializeSeed` method is used to initialize the seed value for the random number generator, and the `getStoredSeed` method is used to retrieve a previously stored seed value from the external database system.

Comprehensive unit tests are also included to validate the functionality of the class and ensure maintainability and code organization. The tests cover edge cases such as invalid seeds, out-of-range values, and the behavior under high-frequency requests.

