The code also includes error handling for various conditions, such as invalid input types, network errors, and edge cases where the hostname might be empty or contain non-numeric values. The function returns an error code if DNS resolution fails or encounters any other issues.

To optimize performance, the function splits the DNS resolution task into smaller chunks and processes them concurrently using asynchronous operations. This allows the function to handle multiple hostnames simultaneously, improving overall performance. The function also properly closes any open connections to the external service after the resolution process is complete.

