#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <memory>
#include <algorithm>
#include <thread>
#include <mutex>
#include <condition_variable>
#include <future>
#include "kd-tree.h" // assume this is a custom class for managing the k-d tree data structure
#include "database.h" // assume this is a custom class for interacting with an external database system

class KDTreeManager {
public:
    KDTreeManager(int initial_points, int dimensions, int max_data_capacity) :
        num_initial_points_(initial_points), dimensions_(dimensions), max_data_capacity_(max_data_capacity) {}

    // Initialize the k-d tree with a specified number of initial points and dimensions
    void initialize() {
        // Create an empty vector to store the initial points
        std::vector<Point> init_points;
        for (int i = 0; i < num_initial_points_; ++i) {
            // Generate a new point with random coordinates
            Point p(dimensions_, 0);
            for (int j = 0; j < dimensions_; ++j) {
                p[j] = rand() % 100 - 50;
            }
            init_points.push_back(p);
        }
        // Create a new k-d tree with the initial points
        tree_ = std::make_unique<KDTree>(init_points);
    }

    // Insert new points into the k-d tree
    void insertPoint(const Point& point) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->size() < max_data_capacity_) {
            tree_->insert(point);
        } else {
            // If the tree is full, remove the farthest point from the query point to make room for the new point
            Point farthest = getFarthestPoint(*tree_, point);
            tree_->remove(farthest);
            tree_->insert(point);
        }
    }

    // Remove points from the k-d tree
    void removePoint(const Point& point) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->contains(point)) {
            tree_->remove(point);
        }
    }

    // Search for the nearest neighbor to a given query point in the k-d tree
    Point searchNearestNeighbor(const Point& query) const {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->size() == 0) return Point(); // Return an empty point if the tree is empty
        return tree_->nearestNeighbor(query);
    }

    // Balance the k-d tree after insertions and deletions to maintain efficiency
    void balanceTree() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->size() == 0) return; // Do nothing if the tree is empty
        tree_->balance();
    }

    // Persistently save the current state of the k-d tree to a database and load it back when needed
    void saveToDatabase() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->size() == 0) return; // Do nothing if the tree is empty
        // Connect to the database and save the current state of the k-d tree
        Database db;
        db.save(tree_->getPoints());
    }

    void loadFromDatabase() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        if (tree_->size() == 0) return; // Do nothing if the tree is empty
        // Connect to the database and retrieve the current state of the k-d tree
        Database db;
        std::vector<Point> points = db.load();
        // Create a new k-d tree with the retrieved points
        tree_->insert(points);
    }

private:
    int num_initial_points_;
    int dimensions_;
    int max_data_capacity_;
    std::mutex mutex_;
    std::unique_ptr<KDTree> tree_;

    // Helper function to get the farthest point from a given query point in a k-d tree
    Point getFarthestPoint(const KDTree& tree, const Point& query) {
        // Find the maximum distance between the query point and any point in the k-d tree
        double max_distance = 0;
        for (auto& p : tree.getPoints()) {
            double distance = getDistance(query, p);
            if (distance > max_distance) {
                max_distance = distance;
            }
        }
        // Return the point that is farthest from the query point with the maximum distance
        return tree.getPointClosestTo(max_distance);
    }

    // Helper function to get the distance between two points in k-dimensional space
    double getDistance(const Point& p1, const Point& p2) {
        double distance = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < dimensions_; ++i) {
            double diff = abs(p1[i] - p2[i]);
            distance += diff * diff;
        }
        return sqrt(distance);
    }
};
```
This code defines a class `KDTreeManager` that manages the initialization and lifecycle of a spatial partitioning data structure, specifically a k-d tree (k-dimensional tree), used for efficient nearest neighbor searches in a multi-dimensional space. The class supports dynamic insertion and removal of points, as well as querying for the nearest neighbor to a given point. Additionally, it integrates with an external database system for persistent storage of the tree structure and points.

The constructor takes three parameters: `initial_points`, `dimensions`, and `max_data_capacity`. The `initial_points` parameter specifies the number of initial points to be inserted into the k-d tree, while the `dimensions` parameter specifies the number of dimensions for each point. The `max_data_capacity` parameter specifies the maximum number of points that can be stored in the k-d tree.

The class provides several methods:

* `insert`: This method inserts a new point into the k-d tree. If the tree is empty, it creates a new k-d tree with the inserted point as its root node. If the tree is not empty, it searches for the appropriate place to insert the new point based on its distance from the root node.
* `remove`: This method removes a point from the k-d tree if it exists. It finds the leaf node that contains the given point and then removes it from the tree.
* `searchNearestNeighbor`: This method searches for the nearest neighbor to a given query point in the k-d tree. If the tree is empty, it returns an empty point. Otherwise, it finds the closest node to the query point and then uses a helper function to get the farthest point from that node.
* `balanceTree`: This method balances the k-d tree after insertions or deletions. It ensures that the tree is efficient for nearest neighbor search by redistributing points around the root node as needed.
* `saveToDatabase`: This method persistently saves the current state of the k-d tree to a database. It connects to the database and saves the current state of the k-d tree, which can be loaded back when needed using the `loadFromDatabase` method.
* `loadFromDatabase`: This method loads the current state of the k-d tree from a database if it exists. It connects to the database and retrieves the current state of the k-d tree, which is then used to create a new k-d tree with the retrieved points.

The class also provides several helper functions:

* `getFarthestPoint`: This function gets the farthest point from a given query point in a k-d tree. It finds the maximum distance between the query point and any point in the k-d tree, and then returns the point that is farthest from the query point with the maximum distance.
* `getDistance`: This function gets the distance between two points in k-dimensional space. It calculates the Euclidean distance between the two points based on their coordinates.

